WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.667
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show"!

00:00:02.667 --> 00:00:04.200
You're here. You're watching.

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:06.267
Big show tonight.

00:00:06.267 --> 00:00:07.901
Let's get to some news.

00:00:07.901 --> 00:00:09.133
First, you guys, this weekend

00:00:09.133 --> 00:00:11.501
was Queen Elizabeth's
platinum jubilee.

00:00:11.501 --> 00:00:15.133
That's right. Britain marked
the Queen's 70-year reign with

00:00:15.133 --> 00:00:18.000
four days of parades, parties,
and celebrations.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.467
Yeah, four days.

00:00:19.467 --> 00:00:21.667
Basically, the Queen is like
your annoying friend who insists

00:00:21.667 --> 00:00:23.167
on celebrating
their "birthday month."

00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:25.334
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.334 --> 00:00:28.234
Yep, the Queen celebrated 70
years of sitting on the throne.

00:00:28.234 --> 00:00:30.567
When he heard, your uncle
who does "The New York Times"

00:00:30.567 --> 00:00:32.801
Sunday crossword puzzle said,
"Challenge accepted."

00:00:32.801 --> 00:00:34.834
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:36.934
It was a star-studded event
with performances from

00:00:36.934 --> 00:00:39.868
Elton John, Rod Stewart,
and Ed Sheeran.

00:00:39.868 --> 00:00:42.000
Yeah, when Ed first walked out,

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.434
the Queen was like,
"Oh, Harry, you're back."

00:00:43.434 --> 00:00:47.234
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.234 --> 00:00:50.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:50.501 --> 00:00:53.400
That's Ed Sheeran.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:57.367
Meanwhile, Prince Andrew did not
attend any festivities

00:00:57.367 --> 00:01:01.000
due to a positive COVID test.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.801
Andrew was like, "It's weird.

00:01:02.801 --> 00:01:05.968
I keep testing positive right
before every public event.

00:01:05.968 --> 00:01:09.200
Can you imagine the odds?"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:11.934
Yep, the Queen made several
appearances this weekend.

00:01:11.934 --> 00:01:13.200
And at one point, she showed up

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:15.601
as her younger self
in the form of a hologram.

00:01:15.601 --> 00:01:17.100
This is real. Check this out.

00:01:18.767 --> 00:01:20.067
Look at this.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:27.767
Yeah. It got confusing
when there was a glitch

00:01:27.767 --> 00:01:29.501
and Tupac started
waving to the crowd.

00:01:29.501 --> 00:01:32.968
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.968 --> 00:01:34.501
But the carriage ride wasn't

00:01:34.501 --> 00:01:36.033
Queen Elizabeth's
only surprise appearance.

00:01:36.033 --> 00:01:39.701
She also starred in a short film
having tea with Paddington Bear.

00:01:39.701 --> 00:01:42.200
It's really cute. It's real.
Take a look.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:46.067
-Perhaps you would like
a marmalade sandwich.

00:01:46.067 --> 00:01:49.033
I always keep one
for emergencies.

00:01:49.033 --> 00:01:51.601
-So do I.

00:01:51.601 --> 00:01:54.501
I keep mine in here.

00:01:54.501 --> 00:01:55.934
-I love that. Come on.

00:01:55.934 --> 00:01:57.701
She's the best. It's so fun.

00:01:57.701 --> 00:01:59.734
It went much better than
Paddington's meeting

00:01:59.734 --> 00:02:00.901
with another world leader.

00:02:00.901 --> 00:02:02.300
Watch this.

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:04.734
-Thank you for the sandwich.

00:02:04.734 --> 00:02:09.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:13.400
But I'd prefer it if
you took the first bite.

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:15.067
-Yeah, yeah, very smart.

00:02:15.067 --> 00:02:16.701
Very smart, Paddington.

00:02:16.701 --> 00:02:17.667
I wouldn't -- I wouldn't --

00:02:17.667 --> 00:02:21.234
[ Applause ]

00:02:21.234 --> 00:02:23.667
Yeah, it was a four-day event
honoring the Queen,

00:02:23.667 --> 00:02:27.234
but it was 4-year-old
Prince Louis who stole the show.

00:02:27.234 --> 00:02:29.100
Here he is at yesterday's
pageant parade.

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:30.467
Look at this.

00:02:38.901 --> 00:02:42.033
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.033 --> 00:02:43.934
-Oh, my God!

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:50.400
-After 20 minutes,
Kate was just like,

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:52.133
"Just hand him the royal iPad,
please."

00:02:52.133 --> 00:02:54.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.234 --> 00:02:56.434
Now when Kate says,
"Yeah, he's a real prince,"

00:02:56.434 --> 00:02:57.901
people know she's being
sarcastic.

00:02:57.901 --> 00:02:58.968
[ Laughter ]

00:02:58.968 --> 00:03:00.968
That's right,
Prince Louis' antics were

00:03:00.968 --> 00:03:02.901
going viral all weekend.

00:03:02.901 --> 00:03:04.434
Here's one photo here.

00:03:04.434 --> 00:03:05.801
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.801 --> 00:03:07.133
Looks like he's gathering
his strength

00:03:07.133 --> 00:03:08.501
for an 8:00 a.m. Zoom meeting.

00:03:08.501 --> 00:03:09.934
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.934 --> 00:03:12.100
Here's Prince Louis
next to the Queen.

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:14.167
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.167 --> 00:03:15.934
That was actually
after she started telling him

00:03:15.934 --> 00:03:17.167
"Top Gun" spoilers.

00:03:17.167 --> 00:03:19.634
He's like, "Don't say Goose,
don't say Goose."

00:03:19.634 --> 00:03:22.000
And, of course,
there's this one here.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:25.701
That's him pretending he's
a passenger on Spirit Airlines.

00:03:25.701 --> 00:03:27.167
That's very interesting.

00:03:27.167 --> 00:03:29.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.534 --> 00:03:33.300
Switching gears, there are
rumors swirling around

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:35.601
the Vatican that Pope Francis
might soon announce

00:03:35.601 --> 00:03:37.434
his retirement.

00:03:37.434 --> 00:03:39.400
When asked what he's going to do
next, the Pope said,

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:40.801
"Greeter de Walmart."

00:03:40.801 --> 00:03:42.634
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.634 --> 00:03:45.367
Yeah, at his age, Pope Francis
said that he could either retire

00:03:45.367 --> 00:03:47.667
or become quarterback of
the Tampa Bay Buccaneers.

00:03:47.667 --> 00:03:49.801
That's interesting.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.801 --> 00:03:51.434
You guys hear about this?

00:03:51.434 --> 00:03:54.033
The new head of CNN said that
the network is going to stop

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:56.133
using the "breaking news"
banner.

00:03:56.133 --> 00:03:58.334
They said they use it too much.
He's got a point.

00:03:58.334 --> 00:03:59.801
They do use it quite a bit.

00:03:59.801 --> 00:04:02.300
If you don't believe me, take
a look at some of the stories

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:04.267
they classified as
breaking news today.

00:04:04.267 --> 00:04:06.000
First, there was this.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:09.801
"Poll says 54% of Americans do
something the other 46% don't."

00:04:09.801 --> 00:04:11.467
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.467 --> 00:04:12.934
-Breaking news?
-That's breaking news.

00:04:12.934 --> 00:04:15.300
-Yeah.
-There was also this story here.

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:17.868
"You know that celebrity who was
dating that other celebrity?

00:04:17.868 --> 00:04:19.501
Well, now she's dating
a different celebrity."

00:04:19.501 --> 00:04:21.567
[ Laughter ]
These aren't breaking --

00:04:21.567 --> 00:04:23.501
And finally, this one says,

00:04:23.501 --> 00:04:27.400
"Glenn holding steady at 547th
most popular baby name."

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:28.567
[ Applause ]

00:04:28.567 --> 00:04:29.667
Breaking news.
-Breaking news.

00:04:29.667 --> 00:04:32.634
-Breaking news,
Glenn with two N's.

00:04:32.634 --> 00:04:35.367
That's right, CNN is trying to
tone things down

00:04:35.367 --> 00:04:36.801
with their "breaking news"
graphics.

00:04:36.801 --> 00:04:40.067
Meanwhile, MSNBC is going in
the exact opposite direction.

00:04:40.067 --> 00:04:42.000
Yep. Check out what I saw
this morning.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:44.200
Watch their breaking-news alert
on MSNBC.

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:46.968
-Breaking news, bitches!
[ Explosions ]

00:04:46.968 --> 00:04:48.100
-You know what I'm saying?
-Wow.

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:50.367
-It's the opposite.
-It gets your attention.

00:04:50.367 --> 00:04:52.601
-I was nervous.

00:04:52.601 --> 00:04:56.367
It was just that Glenn was the
547th most popular baby name.

00:04:56.367 --> 00:04:57.501
-That's breaking news.

00:04:57.501 --> 00:04:58.601
Bitches.

00:04:58.601 --> 00:05:02.467
[ Laughter ]

00:05:02.467 --> 00:05:03.968
-Listen to this, guys.

00:05:03.968 --> 00:05:06.734
Apple just announced a new
feature that will allow people

00:05:06.734 --> 00:05:08.567
to edit and unsend messages.

00:05:08.567 --> 00:05:10.334
[ Audience oohs ]

00:05:10.334 --> 00:05:12.167
When they heard, Apple users
were like, "Finally.

00:05:12.167 --> 00:05:13.567
What the duck took you so long?"

00:05:13.567 --> 00:05:16.701
You know?
[ Laughter ]

00:05:16.701 --> 00:05:18.801
Yep, you can now unsend
messages.

00:05:18.801 --> 00:05:20.634
Now everyone gets to play
that fun game,

00:05:20.634 --> 00:05:22.167
"Did they see it
before I deleted it?"

00:05:22.167 --> 00:05:24.033
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:24.033 --> 00:05:25.934
Well, hey, get this.
According to a new study,

00:05:25.934 --> 00:05:29.467
the actors whose names we
mispronounce the most are

00:05:29.467 --> 00:05:32.601
Saoirse Ronan, Joaquin Phoenix,
and Ewan McGregor.

00:05:32.601 --> 00:05:34.701
-Come on, those are easy.

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:38.667
I've never mispronounced
any actor's names.

00:05:38.667 --> 00:05:41.367
It's my job, you know.
Go ahead, try me.

00:05:41.367 --> 00:05:44.400
-You want me to test you on how
to pronounce actor's names?

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:46.000
-Mm-hmm.
-Okay.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:48.167
Well, we'll start out simple.
Who's this next to you?

00:05:48.167 --> 00:05:49.400
-Oh, that's easy.

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:51.167
Samuel LaJackson.

00:05:51.167 --> 00:05:54.834
[ Laughter ]

00:05:54.834 --> 00:05:57.400
-Okay. Who's this?

00:05:57.400 --> 00:05:58.934
-Robot Diner.

00:05:58.934 --> 00:06:00.701
Come on, give me some hard ones,
man.

00:06:00.701 --> 00:06:02.200
-You want rapid --
-Rapid-fire me.

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:03.501
-You want rapid fire?
-Fire away, man.

00:06:03.501 --> 00:06:05.200
-I'm not sure
this is a great idea.

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:06.667
Alright. Here we go.
Let's just start rolling.

00:06:06.667 --> 00:06:08.200
Who's this?
-Easy. Cate Blanket.

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:09.434
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:09.434 --> 00:06:10.501
-Eighteen Bananas.

00:06:10.501 --> 00:06:11.901
-Mnh-mnh.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:11.901 --> 00:06:14.067
-French Fries McDonald.
-No.

00:06:14.067 --> 00:06:16.601
-Batman Riddler.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:16.601 --> 00:06:18.300
Leggo My Eggo.

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:20.133
Penn and Teller.

00:06:20.133 --> 00:06:22.334
Oh, that's Been Eatin' Del Taco.

00:06:22.334 --> 00:06:24.501
Gilligan's Island.

00:06:24.501 --> 00:06:25.801
Itchy Dandruff.

00:06:25.801 --> 00:06:27.501
Tennis Elbow.

00:06:27.501 --> 00:06:30.300
Shining Taint.

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:32.667
He'll Want To Bone In The Car.

00:06:32.667 --> 00:06:34.801
Oh, I love this guy.
Love this guy. Colon Birth.

00:06:34.801 --> 00:06:36.334
-Alright, that's very good.

00:06:36.334 --> 00:06:38.534
Steve Higgins, everybody.
Very talented.

00:06:38.534 --> 00:06:40.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:41.367
Very talented.

00:06:41.367 --> 00:06:43.467
-Glenn.

00:06:43.467 --> 00:06:46.067
-Hey, guys, I read about a theme
park in Pennsylvania where

00:06:46.067 --> 00:06:49.367
a ride malfunctioned and left
passengers stuck upside-down.

00:06:49.367 --> 00:06:50.868
[ Audience ohs ]

00:06:50.868 --> 00:06:52.634
They couldn't fix it, so they
just said the theme of the ride

00:06:52.634 --> 00:06:53.767
was "Stranger Things."

00:06:53.767 --> 00:06:55.968
[ Laughter ]

00:06:55.968 --> 00:06:59.200
This went viral. Two women
in England were relaxing on

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:01.501
an oversized chair, and they
realized that they

00:07:01.501 --> 00:07:03.100
couldn't get out.
Watch this.

00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:06.634
-Jesus Christ!

00:07:06.634 --> 00:07:09.133
Jes-- Use your crutch, Sue.

00:07:09.133 --> 00:07:12.000
Use your crutch.
Use your crutch.

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:13.968
Jesus, Sue, give her
your crutch.

00:07:13.968 --> 00:07:15.100
Use your crutch.

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:19.067
[ Laughter ]
Use your crutch.

00:07:19.067 --> 00:07:21.434
-In all fairness to Sue,
it really does look like

00:07:21.434 --> 00:07:23.367
she's using her crutch
as hard as she can.

00:07:23.367 --> 00:07:24.567
[ Laughter ]

00:07:24.567 --> 00:07:26.300
Fake friends help you
out of a chair.

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:27.901
Real friends film you, laugh,

00:07:27.901 --> 00:07:30.367
and then post the video
on the Internet.

00:07:30.367 --> 00:07:32.634
Anyway, they live there now.
[ Laughter ]

